   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Truchet Flip\n\nA grid of quarter-circle tiles flips in waves, then settles into a clean pattern: rings, a field or a silhouette.\n\nCategory: backgrounds. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A calm, rule-based pattern background should animate in and settle into a deliberate graphic.\n- A bold geometric title card, transition or intro needs a tile grid that flips into order.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need an organic, noisy texture rather than a crisp grid.\n- The background must keep moving forever: the pattern settles and holds.\n\nVariables:\n- tiles (number, 4-24): Tiles, default 10\n- weight (number, 0.04-0.34): Weight, default 0.2\n- passes (number, 0-4): Passes, default 2\n- wave_mode (enum): Wave mode, default \"radial\"\n- resolve (enum): Resolve, default \"rings\"\n- variant (enum): Variant, default \"stroke\"\n- color (color): Line color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- secondary_color (string): Secondary color, default \"\"\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#002fa7\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 1\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
